{"data": {"id": "10.48550/arxiv.2504.16453", "type": "dois", "attributes": {"doi": "10.48550/arxiv.2504.16453", "prefix": "10.48550", "suffix": "arxiv.2504.16453", "identifiers": [{"identifier": "2504.16453", "identifierType": "arXiv"}], "alternateIdentifiers": [{"alternateIdentifierType": "arXiv", "alternateIdentifier": "2504.16453"}], "creators": [{"name": "Oh, Yong-Geun", "nameType": "Personal", "givenName": "Yong-Geun", "familyName": "Oh", "affiliation": [], "nameIdentifiers": []}], "titles": [{"title": "Leafwise de Rham cohomology of generic Reeb foliations"}], "publisher": "arXiv", "container": {}, "publicationYear": 2025, "subjects": [{"lang": "en", "subject": "Symplectic Geometry (math.SG)", "subjectScheme": "arXiv"}, {"subject": "FOS: Mathematics", "subjectScheme": "Fields of Science and Technology (FOS)"}, {"lang": "en", "subject": "37C86, 53D10, 53D35, 37C05", "subjectScheme": "MSC"}], "contributors": [], "dates": [{"date": "2025-04-23T06:41:47Z", "dateType": "Submitted", "dateInformation": "v1"}, {"date": "2025-04-24T00:24:50Z", "dateType": "Updated", "dateInformation": "v1"}, {"date": "2025-05-12T05:01:40Z", "dateType": "Submitted", "dateInformation": "v2"}, {"date": "2025-05-13T01:10:39Z", "dateType": "Updated", "dateInformation": "v2"}, {"date": "2026-07-16T23:14:04Z", "dateType": "Submitted", "dateInformation": "v3"}, {"date": "2026-07-20T00:11:12Z", "dateType": "Updated", "dateInformation": "v3"}, {"date": "2025-04", "dateType": "Available", "dateInformation": "v1"}], "language": null, "types": {"ris": "GEN", "bibtex": "misc", "citeproc": "article", "schemaOrg": "CreativeWork", "resourceType": "Article", "resourceTypeGeneral": "Preprint"}, "relatedIdentifiers": [], "relatedItems": [], "sizes": [], "formats": [], "version": "3", "rightsList": [{"rights": "arXiv.org perpetual, non-exclusive license", "rightsUri": "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/"}], "descriptions": [{"description": "In this paper, we prove that there exists a residual subset of contact forms $\u03bb$ (if any) on any compact connected orientable manifold $M$ for which the foliation de Rham cohomology of the associated Reeb foliation has $H^0(F_\u03bb) \\cong \\mathbb R$. We also prove the same triviality for a generic choice of contact forms with fixed contact structure $\u03be$. This vanishing result of $H^0(F_\u03bb)$ is also equivalent to the statement that the Lie algebra of the group of strict contactomorphisms is isomorphic to the span of Reeb vector fields, and so isomorphic to the 1 dimensional abelian Lie algebra $\\mathbb R$. On the other hand, we derive the rank of $H^1( F_\u03bb)$ is infinite whenever $\u03bb$ admits a closed Reeb oribt, i.e., whenever Weinstein's conjecture holds. In particular we prove that $H^1(F_\u03bb)$ is infinite dimensional for all contact form $\u03bb$ in dimension 3, thanks to Taubes' proof of 3-dimensional Weinstein's conjecture.", "descriptionType": "Abstract"}, {"description": "37 pages, comments welcome! v2) 55 pages, the case with fixed contact structure added, new perspective on contact dynamics added, exposition much improved; v3) 44 pages, the paper largely rewritten, exposition simplified, more references added, an error concerning the cokernel statement corrected and amplified", "descriptionType": "Other"}], "geoLocations": [], "fundingReferences": [], "xml": "", "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.16453", "contentUrl": null, "metadataVersion": 2, "schemaVersion": "http://datacite.org/schema/kernel-4", "source": "mds", "isActive": true, "state": "findable", "reason": null, "viewCount": 0, "viewsOverTime": [], "downloadCount": 0, "downloadsOverTime": [], "referenceCount": 0, "citationCount": 0, "citationsOverTime": [], "partCount": 0, "partOfCount": 0, "versionCount": 0, "versionOfCount": 0, "created": "2025-04-24T01:48:53.000Z", "registered": "2025-04-24T01:48:54.000Z", "published": "2025", "updated": "2026-07-20T02:20:55.000Z"}, "relationships": {"client": {"data": {"id": "arxiv